# Copy to .env, which is git ignored, and fill in the token. Read by tests/spec/baseline.ps1
# when a batch runs with -Docker, and by nothing the plugin ships.
#
# It is the account every run of a batch logs in as, and running under another one means
# editing this value. Only this key is read, so the file stays the place for whatever other
# credential the repository comes to need.
#
# `claude setup-token` mints a token and wants a Claude subscription, so a batch is billed
# where a session already is instead of on an API key. The token reaches the container in a
# file rather than on the command line, and it is recorded nowhere.

CLAUDE_ACCOUNT=sk-ant-oat01-your-token-here
